1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,015
It does not.

2
00:00:01,015 --> 00:00:07,057
Even the lowest sound we can hear, twenty hertz, squeezes each layer twenty times a second.

3
00:00:07,057 --> 00:00:11,927
At a thousand hertz, a compression lasts only half a millisecond.

4
00:00:11,927 --> 00:00:15,078
And air is a very poor conductor of heat.

5
00:00:15,078 --> 00:00:20,013
So practically no heat leaves a compression, or enters a rarefaction.

6
00:00:20,013 --> 00:00:22,252
The changes are not isothermal.

7
00:00:22,252 --> 00:00:23,671
They are adiabatic.

